1
00:00:16,474 --> 00:00:17,517
Ermes,

2
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,186
how fast are we going right now?

3
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:22,313
Is it 170kph? Or 200kph?

4
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:23,231
What?

5
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:25,734
We're ditching this ride. Emporio!

6
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:34,325
But the first time
I fully caught sight of rods,

7
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,369
it finally dawned on me.

8
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:40,582
The first step on the moon
was made by humanity's willpower.

9
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:44,210
On that same day,
humanity left the Earth and evolved.

10
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:48,214
Mental evolution is invaluable!

11
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:52,385
This is nothing

12
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:54,262
compared to everything else
we've been through.

13
00:00:55,054 --> 00:00:57,474
Compared to finding that priest,

14
00:00:57,557 --> 00:00:59,100
this is nothing.

15
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,104
This bitch!

16
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:07,567
I'm mentally stronger than her.

17
00:01:10,361 --> 00:01:11,571
I'll kill you!

18
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:19,454
Fuck.

19
00:01:22,207 --> 00:01:25,460
- Jolyne!
- Jolyne won!

20
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:29,547
That is why the priest extracted
only his memory

21
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:32,425
and kept him alive all this time.

22
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,803
Weather Forecast.

23
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,391
He is the priest's younger brother.

24
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:43,144
Let's go to Orlando.

25
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,188
We need to go find the priest.

26
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:21,826
EPISODE 28: HEAVEN IS AT HAND:
THREE DAYS UNTIL THE NEW MOON

27
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:22,994
GREEN DOLPHIN STREET PRISON

28
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:24,162
ESCAPED FROM HELICOPTER

29
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,496
ORLANDO

30
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,582
CAPE CANAVERAL
SPACE CENTER

31
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:35,131
ORLANDO, FLORIDA
10 HOURS BY CAR TO CAPE CANAVERAL

32
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:41,054
Hurry! Prepare Emergency Room 3!

33
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:43,806
Male, eight years old.
He's in critical condition.

34
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,600
My baby, Mike!

35
00:03:45,683 --> 00:03:47,602
He will be okay. Everything will be fine.

36
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:52,815
Hey, Jolyne.

37
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:54,734
This is an urgent care facility.

38
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:56,569
Is the priest really hiding here?

39
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:58,279
He's here.

40
00:03:58,863 --> 00:03:59,948
I have no doubt.

41
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:02,367
I don't know why he's here,

42
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:06,329
but this is where we'll settle the score.

43
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:10,333
THREE MORE DAYS UNTIL THE NEW MOON

44
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:12,418
Emporio.

45
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,380
Can you do me a favor?

46
00:04:15,463 --> 00:04:20,009
I want you to deliver my father's disc,
which you've kept safe for us.

47
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:23,554
Call this number,
and the Speedwagon Foundation will come.

48
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,686
I'm going inside with you.

49
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:33,648
Of course you are,
but I want you to deliver the disc first.

50
00:04:33,731 --> 00:04:37,568
The priest must know that
I'm closing in on him.

51
00:04:38,611 --> 00:04:41,030
I don't want to be apart from you,

52
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:42,782
but this is important.

53
00:04:47,537 --> 00:04:49,706
Hold onto this phone we took from Rikiel.

54
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:13,771
Sorry to bother,
but I'd like your opinion.

55
00:05:14,355 --> 00:05:16,149
It concerns this meal.

56
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:20,069
I want you to try it,
if only for a single bite.

57
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,738
Versus.

58
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,789
Try a bite.

59
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:40,506
Tell me the ingredients.

60
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:43,051
I can't eat shellfish.

61
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:45,428
I'm very allergic to them.

62
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:52,977
This is whitefish.

63
00:05:53,811 --> 00:05:55,521
Flounder, to be more precise.

64
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:58,232
It also contains sliced asparagus.

65
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:00,902
The asparagus is incorporated
into some ground crabmeat.

66
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:02,779
It is then steamed like a flan.

67
00:06:03,863 --> 00:06:05,490
There's no shellfish in it.

68
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:07,825
Excellent.

69
00:06:08,409 --> 00:06:09,619
I'm not done.

70
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:13,581
Could I have another bite with the sauce?

71
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,209
I smell something in the sauce.

72
00:06:17,043 --> 00:06:18,920
It may contain ground scallops

73
00:06:19,003 --> 00:06:21,214
mixed in with whipping cream.

74
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:34,018
Unfortunately, it's just as I thought.
There's shellfish in this sauce.

75
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:38,481
So your shoe size is 27cm?

76
00:06:39,273 --> 00:06:41,567
Will you stand up for me?

77
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:47,406
Take your time so that the gunshot wound
on your leg won't open up.

78
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:51,369
Height, 181cm.

79
00:06:52,286 --> 00:06:54,497
Weight, 72kg even.

80
00:06:55,456 --> 00:06:57,375
Size, 52.

81
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:00,461
Watch size is two holes up.

82
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:02,213
Correct.

83
00:07:03,714 --> 00:07:05,341
Interesting.

84
00:07:05,424 --> 00:07:08,261
Though I won't be able to enjoy this dish,

85
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:12,473
you were able to discern
the scallop in the sauce.

86
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:15,726
We share a similar sense of taste.

87
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:27,113
Interesting indeed.

88
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:30,324
Father Pucchi,

89
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,535
what are you hinting at?

90
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:36,205
I haven't seen my ability yet,

91
00:07:36,789 --> 00:07:39,709
while our enemy draws near by the second.

92
00:07:40,751 --> 00:07:42,295
I want to serve you.

93
00:07:43,379 --> 00:07:44,672
What should I do?

94
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:48,801
This can't be helped.

95
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:52,138
That in itself is not a problem.

96
00:07:55,099 --> 00:07:57,435
- Mike…
- Are you okay?

97
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:01,022
He's really close.

98
00:08:01,647 --> 00:08:03,191
He's around here.

99
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:08,779
You haven't seen your ability,
but that can't be helped.

100
00:08:09,655 --> 00:08:14,494
Let the power take its course,
and do not try to resist.

101
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:18,456
Because reaching heaven

102
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,959
means having these factors on our side.

103
00:08:23,002 --> 00:08:26,839
Jolyne may very well forget
to check this room.

104
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:33,221
Anyway, I ordered this item because
it's supposed to be shellfish-free.

105
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:35,556
Feel free to eat it.

106
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,937
Father Pucchi.

107
00:08:42,813 --> 00:08:45,608
I… was…

108
00:08:48,236 --> 00:08:51,447
I was…

109
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:56,369
I was shot.

110
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:59,622
The ambulance was fun.

111
00:08:59,705 --> 00:09:03,209
But my dad hates me.

112
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,336
My dad is the one…

113
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:07,338
who shot me!

114
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:12,802
Honey? Honey!

115
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:14,262
Honey!

116
00:09:14,345 --> 00:09:15,471
He got shot!

117
00:09:18,015 --> 00:09:19,850
Honey, no!

118
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:34,115
This room doesn't look right.

119
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:36,993
Where is the priest?

120
00:09:38,035 --> 00:09:40,246
What is happening?

121
00:09:40,830 --> 00:09:41,998
This situation…

122
00:09:42,498 --> 00:09:46,961
I've no doubt it's the doing
of his new ally.

123
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:51,841
But this doesn't seem like
a Stand ability.

124
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:54,885
He was shot by a real bullet.

125
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,971
And who is he?

126
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:58,639
Who is this man?

127
00:09:58,723 --> 00:10:00,766
Why was he shot?

128
00:10:01,350 --> 00:10:04,312
He's an ordinary citizen!

129
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:09,483
Evacuate everyone on this floor. Hurry!

130
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,818
Y-yes sir.

131
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:14,447
You two over there, evacuate!

132
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:16,449
I'll call the police.

133
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:21,871
I know, the man who got shot!

134
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:24,373
They were the parents of that boy

135
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:26,375
who rushed here in an ambulance!

136
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:28,502
It might be a test shot…

137
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,466
I don't know what the ability is about,

138
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,385
but it could be a newly awakened ability.

139
00:10:36,469 --> 00:10:38,971
If so, the user would want
to know what it is

140
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,890
by testing it out.

141
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:46,145
What's this?

142
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:52,985
They're on the move.

143
00:10:53,569 --> 00:10:54,570
The priest is on the run!

144
00:10:55,154 --> 00:10:57,073
He's inside this hole.

145
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:59,283
I can sense him moving away.

146
00:11:08,584 --> 00:11:10,086
Listen Jolyne.

147
00:11:10,169 --> 00:11:12,588
Don't you dare go down that hole.

148
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:15,132
Got that? I won't allow it.

149
00:11:15,216 --> 00:11:17,093
This is obviously a trap!

150
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:22,348
We need to find out the connection
between this hole and the shooting.

151
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:23,933
Until then, stay away from this hole!

152
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:37,655
The hole goes sideways
to the hospital courtyard.

153
00:11:37,738 --> 00:11:39,240
I can't see any further.

154
00:11:42,493 --> 00:11:44,662
The enemy that's with the priest…

155
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:48,082
His name is Versus.
Twenty-five years old, male.

156
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:49,708
Listen, Jolyne.

157
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:53,045
I'll say this again.
We won't go down this hole.

158
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:54,755
We'll either wait for them to come out

159
00:11:54,839 --> 00:11:57,383
or chase them out like rabbits.

160
00:11:57,466 --> 00:12:01,137
Yes, this hole is an obvious trap.

161
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:04,014
But what if the priest

162
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:07,351
waits three more days in this hole,
until the new moon rises?

163
00:12:08,352 --> 00:12:10,980
Yes, the priest would do just that.

164
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:14,859
He may even use this hole
to reach Cape Canaveral.

165
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:17,987
In three days,
the priest will attain the power

166
00:12:18,070 --> 00:12:21,198
that he calls "reaching heaven."

167
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:23,993
As of now, the priest's ability is limited

168
00:12:24,076 --> 00:12:26,996
to Pale Snake, which manipulates memories.

169
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,873
We can still win.

170
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,459
This is our only chance to stop him.

171
00:12:32,042 --> 00:12:33,294
We'll put him out of commission,

172
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:36,630
or if things turn bleak,
we may even have to kill him.

173
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:39,216
Hold on to this.

174
00:12:40,676 --> 00:12:42,428
Don't ever let go.

175
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,431
Hey, Jolyne!

176
00:12:45,514 --> 00:12:47,308
What are you doing? I'm coming with you!

177
00:12:49,059 --> 00:12:51,896
If you come with me,
then who's going to pull me out?

178
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:54,815
Wrap my thread around your body.

179
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,567
I'll send a signal if I'm in danger.

180
00:12:56,650 --> 00:12:59,695
In that case,
do whatever it takes to pull me up.

181
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:04,074
This is crazy. It's Jolyne's thread.

182
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:08,621
How far can she actually go
while emitting this from her body?

183
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:22,885
Jolyne?

184
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,012
Jolyne!

185
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:27,181
Why won't you answer me?

186
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:28,766
Jolyne!

187
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,697
This place…

188
00:13:49,245 --> 00:13:50,955
STAND NAME: NETHERWORLD
STAND MASTER: DONATELLO VERSUS

189
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,791
This place…

190
00:13:57,878 --> 00:13:59,296
2005?

191
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:01,131
What's going on?

192
00:14:08,055 --> 00:14:09,848
Look, it's her.

193
00:14:09,932 --> 00:14:11,684
She's tied to her thread.

194
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:14,728
I'll go cut it.

195
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:17,815
What is this place?

196
00:14:18,941 --> 00:14:21,902
Ermes, it's not looking good.
Can you hear me?

197
00:14:22,486 --> 00:14:23,696
Pull me up!

198
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:26,949
Hurry, Ermes! This is bad.

199
00:14:27,032 --> 00:14:29,410
Get me out of here. They'll cut my thread!

200
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:39,336
Ermes, what's taking you so long?

201
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:42,256
Hurry, Ermes!

202
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,717
Pull me up!

203
00:14:46,218 --> 00:14:47,469
Ermes!

204
00:14:48,929 --> 00:14:51,015
You should be able to hear me!

205
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:59,356
Dammit, what's going on in there?

206
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,233
She hasn't gone too deep.

207
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:09,408
Ermes, faster!

208
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,327
Pull me up with all your strength!

209
00:15:22,212 --> 00:15:25,215
I welcome you here,
even with your outside shoes on,

210
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:27,384
and even if you didn't greet me.

211
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:30,721
You may enter my hole as you wish.

212
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:36,143
However, make sure to bring
all of this tightened rope with you.

213
00:15:38,562 --> 00:15:39,939
Stone Ocean!

214
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:53,243
Hey Versus, are you hurt?

215
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:57,665
Unlike you, who just
awakened to a Stand ability,

216
00:15:57,748 --> 00:16:01,502
Jolyne Cujoh has become an adept fighter
at The Green Dolphin.

217
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:04,838
You could say she's a hardened fighter.

218
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:08,926
She won't hesitate to nick a pen
from a passenger.

219
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:12,012
Don't bother with Jolyne.

220
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:14,974
You've done excellently, Versus.

221
00:16:15,599 --> 00:16:19,186
If Jolyne wants out, let her leave.

222
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:23,649
She won't try to set foot
in this hole a second time.

223
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:27,444
For the next three days,
we will bide our time in this hole.

224
00:16:27,528 --> 00:16:28,654
That will do.

225
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:33,492
Can you hear me, Ermes? I see the light!

226
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:36,829
I'm close to the exit. Pull me up!

227
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,915
I can hear you, Jolyne!

228
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:43,252
I caught a glimpse of you just now.
Are you hurt?

229
00:16:43,836 --> 00:16:46,213
What did you find down there?

230
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:48,549
The enemy is looking up at me from below.

231
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:52,469
But I also saw the priest down here.

232
00:16:52,553 --> 00:16:55,097
We have to think of other ways
to enter this hole.

233
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,433
I would've been dead
if they cut off my thread.

234
00:17:05,649 --> 00:17:08,110
Now talk to me, will you?

235
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:11,780
Huh, Ermes?

236
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:15,075
How do you feel right now?

237
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:21,165
You buried me alive
in a prison sewage pipe.

238
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:27,755
How did it feel when
you finally avenged your sister?

239
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:30,716
Sports Maximum!

240
00:17:32,926 --> 00:17:35,637
What's going on, Ermes? Get it together!

241
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:37,973
Jolyne!

242
00:17:40,142 --> 00:17:43,395
The Earth records the past.

243
00:17:43,479 --> 00:17:45,272
It's like a magnetic tape,

244
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:47,566
or a digital camera.

245
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,778
It remembers the little boy

246
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:53,572
who fell to the ground
after being shot by his father.

247
00:17:53,655 --> 00:17:55,657
Where the hell did you come from?

248
00:17:55,741 --> 00:18:00,245
It remembers a gangster
who was buried alive in a pipe.

249
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:04,792
It also remembers every detail
of July 2005, seven years ago,

250
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:10,005
when a commercial flight crashed
into the ground.

251
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:13,509
Ermes, what're you doing up there?

252
00:18:13,592 --> 00:18:14,718
Ermes!

253
00:18:14,802 --> 00:18:16,845
Let go, jerk!

254
00:18:16,929 --> 00:18:19,473
This is Versus's ability.

255
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:23,435
Netherworld excavates.

256
00:18:23,519 --> 00:18:25,312
It unearths memories!

257
00:18:25,395 --> 00:18:28,398
Fucker!

258
00:18:33,779 --> 00:18:36,156
Jolyne!

259
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:43,664
Attention all passengers.

260
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:49,253
It is July 21, 2005,
and time to destination is 21:33.

261
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:51,672
This aircraft will crash to the ground.

262
00:18:51,755 --> 00:18:54,341
Please turn off all electronic devices,

263
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:58,303
and fasten your seatbelt
at your lower waist.

264
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:04,810
Also, the face of the passenger seated
at the rear gets lodged in my stomach,

265
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:09,731
by the crash impact.

266
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:12,025
What's going on?

267
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:14,236
Dammit, where is it?

268
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,363
Search for the exit, Ermes.

269
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:20,701
What is this place? Is this an illusion?

270
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:23,996
It was on the ceiling earlier.
Find the hole where we came from.

271
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:27,457
The walls feel just as hard
as the inside of a real plane.

272
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:28,834
We have to find the exit!

273
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:31,962
Did anyone come to the hospital room?

274
00:19:32,462 --> 00:19:35,215
There was commotion
over the little boy's father,

275
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:37,092
so the police should've come.

276
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:38,468
Didn't you see them?

277
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:42,055
I don't know, but even if they're there,

278
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:45,309
I couldn't hear you outside the hole.

279
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:47,477
Are we in a commercial plane?

280
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:50,772
I didn't see anything like this
from above!

281
00:19:53,942 --> 00:19:56,862
Please do not punch the ceiling.

282
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:59,781
Please sit and wait quietly.

283
00:20:00,699 --> 00:20:03,285
We will crash in less than three minutes.

284
00:20:04,828 --> 00:20:07,039
I want to speak with the pilot.

285
00:20:07,122 --> 00:20:09,791
Have him land the plane immediately.

286
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,419
Take us to the cockpit!

287
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,087
It's no use.

288
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:21,261
We couldn't make an emergency landing.

289
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:24,348
That's why we crashed.

290
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:26,099
What's wrong with her?

291
00:20:27,017 --> 00:20:30,145
We all burned to death.

292
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:32,439
When the plane crashed,

293
00:20:32,522 --> 00:20:34,274
there was an explosion.

294
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:35,901
My body…

295
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:43,742
Excuse me, I asked you to turn off
your electronic devices.

296
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:47,704
This can't be.
I remember hearing about this incident.

297
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:50,540
Flight 2882, en route to Dallas.

298
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:53,919
This plane crashed close to Orlando
six or seven years ago.

299
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:55,671
Are they ghosts…

300
00:20:55,754 --> 00:20:58,423
We're memories,
merely the facts of the event

301
00:20:58,507 --> 00:21:01,468
recorded by the Earth.

302
00:21:01,551 --> 00:21:04,263
Are we seriously about to crash?

303
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:13,272
Can't you speed up the crash?

304
00:21:13,855 --> 00:21:17,109
I've been feeling
Weather Forecast's presence.

305
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:29,288
They are really close to this hospital.

306
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:34,001
Cut the chatter. You confuse me.

307
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:36,878
Are you talking to me?

308
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:44,970
Netherworld unearths memories.

309
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:49,683
The time of the crash was set at 21:33.

310
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:51,560
And please don't forget

311
00:21:51,643 --> 00:21:56,565
that I managed to drag Ermes along.

312
00:21:58,025 --> 00:22:00,360
I did it all for you.

313
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:02,738
Leave this to me.

314
00:22:08,785 --> 00:22:13,540
TWO MINUTES UNTIL CRASH

315
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
